Escape servers named by domain (#s321), and DoH answers for them:

  entry-a  223.5.5.5 answers 198.51.100.66, a `refuse` range in escape-dns.txt
           (the local override), so it has no say; 1.12.12.12 answers
           192.0.2.10 and .11 — used, no probe.
  entry-b  223.5.5.5 answers through a CNAME with 192.0.2.20 and 203.0.113.99;
           escape-dns.txt allows only 192.0.2.0/24 for it, so .99 is refused
           and .20 used (1.12.12.12 has no answer for it: one source). The server is written `Entry-B.example` on purpose:
           names compare in lower case.
  entry-c  223.5.5.5 answers 10.10.10.10 (private), 1.12.12.12 198.18.0.5
           (fake-IP range): refused with nothing kept, so its member resolves
           through dns-escape and gets no address — it fails closed instead
           of dialing a sinkhole.
  beta     an address literal: never resolved, never guarded.

`render` must write escape-dns.tsv and escape-hosts, warn about each refused
answer, give entry-a/b/c the dns-escape domain_resolver and add the hosts
server; `status` (from a fresh sandbox) says none is checked yet.
